# No em / en dashes

Do **not** use Unicode em dash (`—`) or en dash (`–`) in:

- Operator-facing UI strings (labels, hints, notices, toasts, empty states)
- CHANGELOG / Wiki / PR text meant for humans
- Replies to Filip (Polish or English)

Use a comma, period, colon, parentheses, or a plain hyphen-minus (`-`) instead.

```text
Bad:  Search by name — pick a match
Good: Search by name. Pick a match.
Good: Search by name - pick a match
```

Code comments may keep existing dashes; do not introduce new em/en dashes in new comments either.
